"Each particle is a place where a band's frequencies sit in the newest analysis: at the centre of gravity of the speakers, weighted by each frequency's amplitude in each (for one sound panned with gains, the direction of its velocity vector). A sound only one speaker carries sits at that speaker; one panned between speakers sits on the line between them where its gains put it, at every frequency; two sounds sharing a band each keep their own place; sound the speakers carry independently scatters along the lines between them. Neighbouring frequencies at one place share a particle. Energy that cancels between speakers is tinted ochre where it sits. A description of how the feeds share the signal, not a measured sound field or source distance; speakers stand where the speaker layout puts them (the standard one puts every height at 45 degrees). Hover over a particle to read its frequency, level and what places it there." = "Each particle is a place where a band's frequencies sit in the newest analysis: at the centre of gravity of the speakers, weighted by each frequency's amplitude in each (for one sound panned with gains, the direction of its velocity vector). A sound only one speaker carries sits at that speaker; one panned between speakers sits on the line between them where its gains put it, at every frequency; two sounds sharing a band each keep their own place; sound the speakers carry independently scatters along the lines between them. Neighbouring frequencies at one place share a particle. Energy that cancels between speakers is tinted ochre where it sits. A description of how the feeds share the signal, not a measured sound field or source distance; speakers stand where the speaker layout puts them (the standard one puts every height at 45 degrees). Hover over a particle to read its frequency, level and what places it there.";
