/* Radiant body (build 101) */
"Radiant body" = "Radiant body";
"Radiant body places sound by" = "Radiant body places sound by";
"Radiant body draws each band where its frequencies are heard, at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry them weighted by their level in each, as one glowing body: a centred phantom gathers between L and R, a wide stereo programme stretches along the line between them, and sound all round gathers toward the listener. It glows in the frequencies' hues, burns toward white where it is dense and loud, and swells into haze as it ages. Point lights over it mark exactly where each band's frequencies sit. Level body draws the level heard from each direction as the radius of one body, read on the floor's dBFS rings." = "Radiant body draws each band where its frequencies are heard, at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry them weighted by their level in each, as one glowing body: a centred phantom gathers between L and R, a wide stereo programme stretches along the line between them, and sound all round gathers toward the listener. It glows in the frequencies' hues, burns toward white where it is dense and loud, and swells into haze as it ages. Point lights over it mark exactly where each band's frequencies sit. Level body draws the level heard from each direction as the radius of one body, read on the floor's dBFS rings.";
"How bright and dense the body glows." = "How bright and dense the body glows.";
"How far below the loudest band frequencies still add to the body, in dB: the loudest burn white, quieter ones fade out over this range. How loud the loudest band is sets how dense the whole body is. Hover over the body to read a band's level." = "How far below the loudest band frequencies still add to the body, in dB: the loudest burn white, quieter ones fade out over this range. How loud the loudest band is sets how dense the whole body is. Hover over the body to read a band's level.";
"How large each new particle's light is in the body: larger merges neighbouring places into one mass, smaller keeps them apart." = "How large each new particle's light is in the body: larger merges neighbouring places into one mass, smaller keeps them apart.";
"How much light swells as it ages, so older light turns to haze while new light stays compact. 0 keeps it as compact as when it was heard." = "How much light swells as it ages, so older light turns to haze while new light stays compact. 0 keeps it as compact as when it was heard.";
"Frequency colors the body by the frequencies heard at each place, warm bass through cool treble: where many bands meet it burns toward a cream-white core, and its fringes show what dominates there. Theme draws it in the palette's color. A split into 3 or 5 bands always shows each band in its own color." = "Frequency colors the body by the frequencies heard at each place, warm bass through cool treble: where many bands meet it burns toward a cream-white core, and its fringes show what dominates there. Theme draws it in the palette's color. A split into 3 or 5 bands always shows each band in its own color.";
"Draws the analysis' observations as points instead of the body, for checking where sound is placed: the newest frame only, every point the same small size, without smear, glow or depth shading." = "Draws the analysis' observations as points instead of the body, for checking where sound is placed: the newest frame only, every point the same small size, without smear, glow or depth shading.";
"How readily speakers that share coherent energy count as one image. In Radiant body it decides what reads as a phantom image or out of phase (the ochre tint and the pointer's reading), not where the body sits: its frequencies' amplitudes decide that. Coherence is measured from the speakers' smoothed cross-spectra and corrected for chance. The analysis uses it (in the plugin, too)." = "How readily speakers that share coherent energy count as one image. In Radiant body it decides what reads as a phantom image or out of phase (the ochre tint and the pointer's reading), not where the body sits: its frequencies' amplitudes decide that. Coherence is measured from the speakers' smoothed cross-spectra and corrected for chance. The analysis uses it (in the plugin, too).";
"The quietest band drawn: a band below it adds nothing to the body, whatever the glow range." = "The quietest band drawn: a band below it adds nothing to the body, whatever the glow range.";
"How long light stays in the body, fading and swelling as it goes; the longer, the more it builds up into a trail of where sound has been." = "How long light stays in the body, fading and swelling as it goes; the longer, the more it builds up into a trail of where sound has been.";
"A glowing body of the speaker feeds' frequency bands, each where its band is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry it, weighted by its level in each. A centred phantom gathers between two speakers, a wide stereo programme stretches along the line between them, sound all round gathers toward the listener. The loudest band burns white and quieter ones fade out %d dB below it; older light swells into haze. Point lights mark exactly where each band's frequencies sit. Energy out of phase is tinted ochre. Speakers stand where the speaker layout puts them (the standard one puts every height at 45 degrees)." = "A glowing body of the speaker feeds' frequency bands, each where its band is heard: at the centre of gravity of the speakers that carry it, weighted by its level in each. A centred phantom gathers between two speakers, a wide stereo programme stretches along the line between them, sound all round gathers toward the listener. The loudest band burns white and quieter ones fade out %d dB below it; older light swells into haze. Point lights mark exactly where each band's frequencies sit. Energy out of phase is tinted ochre. Speakers stand where the speaker layout puts them (the standard one puts every height at 45 degrees).";
"The body wears the colors of the frequencies at each place, warm for bass and cool for treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white." = "The body wears the colors of the frequencies at each place, warm for bass and cool for treble; where many bands meet, their light adds up toward white.";
"This plugin sends no frequencies of its own (before build 87), so Radiant body draws from the spatial field's statistics. Install the plugins of this build to see each frequency where it is heard." = "This plugin sends no frequencies of its own (before build 87), so Radiant body draws from the spatial field's statistics. Install the plugins of this build to see each frequency where it is heard.";
"Points" = "Points";
"How bright the point lights over the body are: each is one place where a band's frequencies are heard, crisp when new and smearing as it ages, so where every band sits can be read exactly. The body dims a little under them, so they carry the brightest light. 0 shows the body alone." = "How bright the point lights over the body are: each is one place where a band's frequencies are heard, crisp when new and smearing as it ages, so where every band sits can be read exactly. The body dims a little under them, so they carry the brightest light. 0 shows the body alone.";

